      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To find the effectiveness of diagnoses of acute precordial pain seen as an emergency at our centre."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "Observational, descriptive and retrospective study."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "Urban primary care centre."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS",
          "content": "The 100 most recent patients who attended as an emergency with their first episode of acute precordial pain were included."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "STUDY PERIOD",
          "content": "December 1994 to March 1998. Home visits, patients without medical records and those seen on repeated attendance for precordialgia were excluded."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "MEASUREMENTS AND MAIN RESULTS",
          "content": "The emergency diagnosis and the diagnosis recorded afterwards in the clinical history of 100 people with acute precordialgia, aged 54.9 (16.7 years; 56% [n = 56] women), were gathered. Ischaemic cardiopathy (41%, n = 41) and mechanical precordialgia (36%, n = 36) were the most common initial diagnoses. We found 66.6% sensitivity and 81.4% specificity in the detection of ischaemic cardiopathy. The proportion of diagnostic errors was not linked to the pathological history of anxiety, ischaemic cardiopathy or oesophageal disease."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "41% of precordialgias are diagnosed as presumably ischaemic and are potentially serious, although only 50% of them are confirmed as such. Our sensitivity in their diagnosis is comparable to that of other studies."
        }
      ]},
